---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import PagedShelf from '../../components/review/PagedShelf.astro';
import {getShelfCatalog} from '../../lib/shelf-catalog';
import operations from '../../data/phase-207-current-operations.json';
import ledger from '../../data/phase-206-editorial-classification.json';
const {classification}=await getShelfCatalog();
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial classification review | FTFN">
  <section class="page-section">
    <h1 class="page-title">Internal tests are not external operating results.</h1>
    <p class="lede">{ledger.individually_reviewed} individual classifications are recorded, including {ledger.corrected_presentations} corrected presentations. {ledger.remaining_individual_reviews > 0 ? `Another ${ledger.remaining_original_cohort_reviews} original candidates and ${ledger.remaining_additional_cohort_reviews} additional workflow-origin records require individual review.` : 'All screened signal records now have individual classifications. Briefing/research-document review and production acceptance remain open.'} All {ledger.records.length} current-feed exclusions remain.</p>
    <p>Classification is not a fresh external-source check or independent approval. Historical publication states and indexed URLs remain preserved. A source edit invalidates its pinned classification input and requires re-review before regeneration.</p>
    <p><a href="/data/editorial-classification.json">Download every disposition, original title, source hash and review state</a></p>
    <h2>Why the Amtrak headline changed</h2>
    <p><a href="/signals/57n-amtrak-24-accepted-label-conformance-tests/">FTFN adapter passes 24 Amtrak-label conformance tests</a>. The original title incorrectly attributed internal test passage to Amtrak. The body reported zero real candidate packets or reviewer receipts.</p>
    <h2>Classification archive</h2>
    <p>This is an intentional archive of records excluded from the external-development feed. "Under review" titles quote an unadjudicated historical presentation, not a verified finding. Use the classification filter to distinguish reviewed method notes, research dockets and unresolved records. Review dates are not external observation dates.</p>
    <p>A research docket can combine historical method work with real, separately dated source reviews. The <a href="/signals/57y-preserved-la-starlink-adoption/">Starlink adoption docket</a> preserves its September 1 and September 8 decisions; classification does not turn those receipts into fixtures or establish observed adoption.</p>
    <PagedShelf records={classification} kind="classification" headingLevel={3}/>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>Measured-outcomes pilot review</h2>
    <p>The measurement feature remains held: no series is admitted. These findings identify missing evidence, not project success or failure. This is not an owner-approved scope reduction or a full-v1 pass.</p>
    {operations.pilot_reviews.map(p=>{const latest=operations.pilot_research_followups.filter(r=>r.pilot_id===p.pilot_id&&r.checked_date<=operations.as_of_date).at(-1);return <article class="record-card"><h3>{p.title}</h3>{latest&&<div data-pilot-latest={latest.review_id}><p>{latest.status} · {latest.checked_date}</p><p>{latest.finding}</p><p><strong>Next:</strong> {latest.next_action}</p><a href={`#${latest.review_id}`}>Exact dated findings and missing artifacts</a></div>}<details><summary>Preserved first-pass extraction · {p.reviewed_date}</summary><p>{p.outcome}</p><p>{p.finding}</p><p><strong>Next at that review:</strong> {p.next_action}</p><p><a href={p.artifact_url}>Exact candidate artifact</a></p></details></article>})}
    <p><a href="/data/current-operations.json">Inspect extraction candidates, period conflicts and review limits</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>Evidence backlog: checked research is not an authorized decision</h2>
    <p>{operations.backlog_research_checked} of the 25 prepared records have bounded official-source research checks. Another {operations.backlog_research_unchecked} still await that research. All 25 remain unadjudicated; none has been approved for publication by this pass.</p>
    <ul>{operations.backlog_reviews.map(r => <li><a href={r.route}>{r.title}</a> — {r.finding} Next check {r.next_check_date}; authorized disposition pending.</li>)}</ul>
    <p>Historical source dates remain unchanged. Retrieval failures and incomplete table extraction are documented limits, not absence findings. The dated evidence-cycle gates remain separate.</p>
    <p><a href="/data/current-operations.json">Download the individual research receipts and exact artifact locations</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
